    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110020">Pairing</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110021">Please enter split-screen (multi-window) mode first.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110022">The system requires the pairing dialog always visible, using split-screen mode is the only way to let this app and system dialog visible at the same time.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110023">Enter the code in the notification to complete pairing.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110024">Back to Shizuku and start Shizuku.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110025">Please note, left part of the \"Wireless debugging\" option is clickable, tapping it will open a new page. Only turing on the switch on the right is incorrect.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110026">MIUI users may need to switch notification style to \"Android\" from \"Notification\" - \"Notification shade\" in system settings.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110027">Otherwise, you may not able to enter paring code from the notification.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110028">Shizuku needs to access local network. It is controlled by the network permission.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f110029">Some systems (such as MIUI) disallow apps to access the network when they are not visible, even if the app uses foreground service as standard. Please disable battery optimization features for Shizuku on such systems.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f11002a">A notification from Shizuku will help you complete the pairing.</string>
    <string name="APKTOOL_RENAMED_0x7f11002b">The pairing process needs you to interact with a notification from Shizuku. Please allow Shizuku to post notifications.</string>
